Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bdzlr/bdnzlr do not end a function

- The function analysis took a bclr whose BO has 0x10 set (ignore the
  condition) as an unconditional blr. bdzlr/bdnzlr have 0x10 set too, but
  they decrement CTR and fall through when it isn't zero: only
  BO & 0x14 == 0x14 is unconditional.
- HP: Deathly Hallows - Part 1's CRT memset (sub_82355E40, a leaf with no
  .pdata) ends in "stb; bdzlr; stb; bdzlr; stb; blr". The function was cut
  after the first bdzlr, so a memset whose tail after the last word is 2 or 3
  bytes left the last 1-2 bytes unset. Wwise's random containers then started
  with stale "blocked" bits, picked items past the end of their playlists and
  wrote past their bit arrays: heap corruption in Wwise's pool and the crash
  after 3-4 minutes of combat.
---
--- a/XenonAnalyse/function.cpp
+++ b/XenonAnalyse/function.cpp
@@ -180,8 +180,10 @@
                 }
                 else if (op == PPC_OP_CTR)
                 {
-                    // 5th bit of BO tells cpu to ignore the counter, which is a blr/bctr otherwise it's conditional
-                    const bool conditional = !(PPC_BO(instruction) & 0x10);
+                    // Unconditional only when BO ignores both the condition (0x10)
+                    // and the counter (0x04): bdzlr/bdnzlr (BO 1a01t/1a00t) decrement
+                    // CTR and fall through when it isn't zero.
+                    const bool conditional = (PPC_BO(instruction) & 0x14) != 0x14;
                     if (conditional)
                     {
                         // right block's just going to return
